	"variations": [
		{
			"statement": "Dans un repère, on considère la parabole $\\mathcal{P}$ d'équation $y={{eval:a*x^2+b*x+c}}$.\n\nLa droite d'équation $x={{eval:k}}$ coupe $\\mathcal{P}$ en un seul point. Quelle est son ordonnée ?\n\n$y=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "x",
					"expression": "x|x"
				},
				{
					"name": "a",
					"expression": "-2|-1|1|2"
				},
				{
					"name": "b",
					"expression": "-5..5"
				},
				{
					"name": "c",
					"expression": "-6..6"
				},
				{
					"name": "k",
					"expression": "-3..3"
				}
			],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:a*k^2+b*k+c}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"Le point commun a pour abscisse ${{eval:k}}$ : son ordonnée est l'image de ${{eval:k}}$.",
					"$y={{eval:a}}\\times{{eval:k;()}}^2{{eval:b;+}}\\times{{eval:k;()}}{{eval:c;+}}=\\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{{{eval:a*k^2+b*k+c}}}$."
				]
			},
			"conditions": ["b != 0", "c != 0", "k != 0"]
		},
		{
			"statement": "Dans un repère, on considère la parabole $\\mathcal{P}$ d'équation $y={{eval:a*x^2-a*(u+v)*x+a*u*v+k}}$.\n\nLa droite d'équation $y={{eval:k}}$ coupe $\\mathcal{P}$ en deux points. Quelle est la plus grande de leurs abscisses ?\n\n$x=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "x",
					"expression": "x|x"
				},
				{
					"name": "a",
					"expression": "-2|-1|1|2"
				},
				{
					"name": "u",
					"expression": "-4..4"
				},
				{
					"name": "v",
					"expression": "-4..4"
				},
				{
					"name": "k",
					"expression": "-5..5"
				}
			],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:v}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"Les points communs vérifient ${{eval:a*x^2-a*(u+v)*x+a*u*v+k}}={{eval:k}}$, soit ${{eval:a*x^2-a*(u+v)*x+a*u*v}}=0$.",
					"Ce trinôme a pour racines ${{eval:u}}$ et ${{eval:v}}$ (discriminant, ou factorisation ${{eval:a*(x-u)*(x-v)}}$).",
					"La plus grande abscisse est $\\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{{{eval:v}}}$."
				]
			},
			"conditions": ["u < v", "u != 0", "v != 0", "k != 0", "u*v + k != 0", "u + v != 0"]
		},
		{
			"statement": "Dans un repère, on considère la parabole $\\mathcal{P}$ d'équation $y={{eval:a*x^2-2*a*s*x+a*s^2+m}}$.\n\nCombien la droite d'équation $y={{eval:k}}$ a-t-elle de points communs avec $\\mathcal{P}$ ?\n\n$?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "x",
					"expression": "x|x"
				},
				{
					"name": "a",
					"expression": "-2|-1|1|2"
				},
				{
					"name": "s",
					"expression": "-4..4"
				},
				{
					"name": "m",
					"expression": "-5..5"
				},
				{
					"name": "k",
					"expression": "-5..5"
				}
			],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:1+sign(a*(k-m))}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"$y={{eval:a*x^2-2*a*s*x+a*s^2+m}}={{eval:a*(x-s)^2}}{{eval:m;+}}$ (forme canonique).",
					"Les points communs vérifient ${{eval:a*(x-s)^2}}{{eval:m;+}}={{eval:k}}$, soit $(x{{eval:-s;+}})^2={{eval:(k-m)/a}}$.",
					"Deux solutions si ce nombre est strictement positif, une s'il est nul, aucune sinon : nombre de points communs, $\\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{{{eval:1+sign(a*(k-m))}}}$."
				]
			},
			"conditions": ["s != 0", "m != 0", "a*s^2 + m != 0", "abs(k - m) <= 3"]
		}
	],
